# QR Order — Project Rules

## Product

Fast ordering & payment for hospitality venues (NOT a digital menu). Guests scan QR → order → pay. Staff use dashboard. Owners use admin.

## Stack

Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind 4 + shadcn/ui + Supabase + Stripe Connect + Zustand + pnpm

## Design

Follow [ADR-007](../docs/design/ADR-007-visual-system.md) + [Denis Spatial plan](../docs/design/denis-spatial-implementation-plan.md):
- **Brand**: **Denis** (public) · subline **Part of Vera Group** · tenant name in dashboard
- **Guest app**: Dark luxury (`guest-theme`), ember `#f97316`, Inter
- **Dashboard / Admin / Platform**: Dark pro (`dashboard-theme` / `admin-theme`), same ember accent
- **Admin (legacy)**: Do not add light `neutral-50` / blue primary — use semantic `bg-card`, `text-dash-*`
- **Kitchen**: Dark high-contrast, very large text
- No spinners (skeleton loaders only), 200ms animations, min 48px touch targets

## Conventions

- Price snapshots in `order_items` at order time — never reference live prices
- Daily order numbers via `get_next_order_number()` PostgreSQL function
- QR URLs use `qr_token`, not table ID
- Guest orders/sessions created via API routes with service role
- Stripe Connect account stored on `organizations`, not locations
- Amounts as DECIMAL in DB, cents only for Stripe API

## Route Groups

- `(guest)/[slug]/[token]` — menu, cart, checkout, order tracking
- `(dashboard)/dashboard/*` — staff: orders, kitchen, tables, waiter calls, history
- `(admin)/admin/*` — owner/manager: menu CRUD, tables/QR, staff, analytics, Stripe
- `(auth)` — login, signup, callback

## Build Order

Phase 1 (setup) → Admin (test data) → Guest → Payments → Dashboard/Realtime → KDS → Analytics

